(FMT-25 — a text built from a format string survives being appended to a
 list and carried into an `Execute` argument list: /bin/echo receives it
 as a real NUL-terminated argv entry and echoes it back. This is the
 observable consequence of the "materializes into a fresh NUL-terminated
 string" claim (FMT-23) — before v0.1.17 this path passed a NULL pointer.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox probe.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   echo-arg
)
a text called stem is "echo".
a text called tok is "{stem}-arg".
a list called cmdargs is [].
append tok to cmdargs.
Execute "/bin/echo" with arguments cmdargs.
